  "equipment_type": "Indoor pool dehumidifier (air handler) controller",
  "applies_to": "Desert Aire SelectAire (SA) indoor pool dehumidifiers running controller program version 3.x.x.",
  "summary": "SelectAire units are indoor pool dehumidifiers. The BACnet list is similar to the SelectAire Plus list but uses different instance numbers and a few different points: sensor analog inputs, four writable setpoints, component status and alarm binary inputs, seven writable binary values (occupancy, event, max outdoor air, purge, unit off, roof lockout, reset) and a multistate unit status. Program 3.0.11 added two discharge pressure sensor fault inputs.",
  "bacnet_transport": [],
  "firmware": "Program version 3.x.x (BI 102/103 need 3.0.11 or later)",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "BI 35 Active Alarm is inverted: 0 = alarm active, 1 = normal.",
    "BI 102/103 and MI 102 share instance 102 but are different object types.",
    "BI 48 Remote Off is 0 when the unit is off and 1 in normal operation.",
    "The source does not say whether the unit uses BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP.",
    "The list covers options a given unit may not have (second pool, cooling towers, VOC sensor, circuit B); those points won't carry real data.",
    "The SelectAire Plus (SP) list has similar points at different instance numbers; don't reuse one unit's mapping on the other."
  ],
